{"base_rate":0.1032171581769437,"brier":0.10213310991957104,"bss":-0.10338574340457751,"bss_hi":0.07930770311642925,"bss_lo":-0.43045554552954896,"chart":{"base":[151.2,275.6],"fp":[215.0,34.0],"lead":"62,214.6 272,175 482,151.3 692,124.7","note":{"base":"skill -0.10 — higher than 6% of cities","fp":"low end -0pp, high end +42pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.5 °C — better than 18% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 77% → rained 39%"},"rel":"65.1,462.1 191.5,428.3 545,296.6"},"country":"PK","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.10333780160857908,"ess":447.8201080900476,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Faisalabad</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Faisalabad rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (92%), believe about\n<b>49%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 746 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.10, ranked 202 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(180&ndash;208) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>373</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Faisalabad</b> <span class=\"muted\">Pakistan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;10% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 10% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.10</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>180&ndash;208\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>746 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Faisalabad &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Faisalabad\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 68.76957746478874,356.3661971830986 94.85230769230769,316.6666666666667 170.18309859154928,228.19718309859155 270.4,126.2162162162162 384.7106329113924,27.215189873417728 384.7106329113924,68.68354430379748 270.4,200.12297297297297 170.18309859154928,305.09859154929575 94.85230769230769,368.0 68.76957746478874,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"344.4289544235925\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"344.4289544235925\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,380.0482573726542 68.76957746478874,371.7464788732394 94.85230769230769,354.0 170.18309859154928,346.11267605633805 270.4,278.7027027027027 384.7106329113924,202.30379746835442\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 373 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"380.0482573726542\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.76957746478874\" cy=\"371.7464788732394\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 10%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"94.85230769230769\" cy=\"354.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"170.18309859154928\" cy=\"346.11267605633805\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 60%&amp;#10;It rained 28% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"270.4\" cy=\"278.7027027027027\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"384.7106329113924\" cy=\"202.30379746835442\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(10%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Faisalabad the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.14) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.53).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>-0.535</td><td class='num'>6.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>181</td><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'>-0.519</td><td class='num'>9.0%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'>-0.262</td><td class='num'>22.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>212</td><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'>0.144</td><td class='num'>5.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":31.41554,"lon":73.08969,"n":746,"n_cities":216,"name":"Faisalabad","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":373,"obs":0.005361930294906166,"sig":true},{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.030422535211267608,"n":71,"obs":0.028169014084507043,"sig":false},{"hi":0.19,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.10410256410256409,"n":78,"obs":0.07692307692307693,"sig":false},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.19,"mean":0.3169014084507042,"n":71,"obs":0.09859154929577464,"sig":true},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.45,"mean":0.6,"n":74,"obs":0.28378378378378377,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.9229113924050633,"n":79,"obs":0.4936708860759494,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.2,"provisional":false,"rank":202,"rank_hi":208.0,"rank_lo":179.975,"reliability":0.03405832812703984,"resolution":0.024777002724081138,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"faisalabad","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Karachi"}